  "id": "eval.2026-09-08-reflow-152600.ivr-agent-handoff",
  "title": "Phone support · AI agent handoff",
  "description": "# Phone support · AI agent handoff\nRead down the call-controller intake, then across to AI self-service or human support. The inbound trunk supplies the caller number for lookup before any greeting: a match loads account context; no match or an error gets a generic greeting. Recording and transcription consent precedes the short speech menu, with keypad fallback for noisy or unreliable recognition.\n\nEligible routine intents reach the real-time AI voice agent, which uses a read-only account lookup and limited authorized actions. Resolved calls end; unresolved requests, requests for a person, and low-confidence flags transfer to the human queue. Ineligible intents bypass AI. Human handoff carries transcript, account context, detected intent, and completed work. A wait-target check leads either to a human or a callback offer, scheduled if accepted.\n\nThe blue evidence and quality-review path represents call-wide recordings and transcripts and review of unresolved and abandoned calls. Its dashed feedback updates the allowed AI intents. Consent-declined behavior is not specified and requires a policy decision.",
